  "id": "Compound::DB01136 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Carvedilol is shown to interact with Adra1d, a variant of the Adra1 receptor, which is involved in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. This interaction is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Carvedilol binds to Adra1d and that this binding leads to participation in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. This activity is then associated with Adra1b, suggesting a potential role for Adra1d in the functional activation of Adra1b. The evidence suggests that Carvedilol may influence Adra1b through a mechanism involving Adra1d, potentially modulating its activity in a context where Alpha-adrenergic signaling is involved. The integration of these paths highlights a possible pathway where Carvedilol exerts its effects on Adra1b via Adra1d, emphasizing the importance of Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity in this relationship.",
